{
  "readme": [
    "Contract fixtures for the Slides grouped composite load (ticket 20, spec 6.2 and 6.6).",
    "The contract itself is the module docstring of suite/slides/api/composite.py.",
    "Ids, timestamps and codes here are placeholders; shapes, ordering and counts are not.",
    "suite/slides/tests/test_composite_groups.py compares a real answer against this file,",
    "and composite-groups.test.ts holds the client to the rules the file states.",
    "The composite names 21 separately shared decks, so it cannot be loaded in one request:",
    "the first group carries the composite's own code plus 19 reference codes, which is the",
    "20 items X-Drive-Links allows. The second group carries only the composite's code, so",
    "both of its references come back marked unreadable, in place, with no content."
  ],
